# the cache is valid only for the exact crawl-common it was made from (each .des file's mtime and the
# save version are in it): the same version here and in Depends
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), crawl (= 2:0.34.1-2), crawl-common (= 2:0.34.1-2)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://crawl.develz.org/

Package: crawl-walnut
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, crawl-tiles, crawl-common (= 2:0.34.1-2)
Description: Dungeon Crawl Stone Soup (tiles), Walnut's start with prebuilt caches
 Dungeon Crawl Stone Soup is a roguelike adventure through dungeons filled with
 monsters in a quest to find the mystifying Orb of Zot. This package adds
 /usr/games/crawl-walnut, which starts Debian's crawl-tiles fullscreen at the
 desktop's resolution (the game's own setting, or a player's rc file, still wins).
 .
 On first start Crawl compiles its 143 vault files and its text database into
 caches in ~/.crawl/saves, which took minutes on the PS3. The caches are made
 when this package is built, from the same crawl-common, and copied into the
 home on start where they are missing, so the first game starts like any other.
